WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.589 --> 00:00:12.299
I was in the Navy for 26 years, and I was
a hospital corpsman. Here's a great opportunity

00:00:12.299 --> 00:00:17.529
for veterans. I know you raised your right
hand and you swore to defend the Constitution

00:00:17.529 --> 00:00:21.750
against all enemies, foreign and domestic.
Would you like to know what that really meant?

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:27.410
Would you like to know those source documents
to federalist papers and read those and understand

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:34.030
what it means to be an American and defend
our Constitution, and get an education that

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:39.160
will propel you forward. Your GI bill is very
valuable and there are a lot of people out

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:44.190
there who would love to take it, but you're
coming to an institution that won't take it.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:49.579
In fact, we're going to supplement your GI
bill with money from Americans who believe

00:00:49.579 --> 00:00:55.320
in liberty, in the Constitution, and they
want you to have this awesome education.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:01:02.320
Why would you not want that? When you leave
the military, you go to the transition assistance

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:07.200
office, and they let you know, they try to
bring you back into the civilian world. We

00:01:07.289 --> 00:01:13.279
know how those civilians can be. Here the
transition is also something that you have

00:01:13.279 --> 00:01:20.279
to go through. And so, we have provided opportunity
for you to transition. We have a dorm that

00:01:20.329 --> 00:01:25.840
we have been housing some of our veterans.
We call it Fort Awesome, and it's awesome.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:32.130
We hook you up with an advisor that was prior
military. You come and talk to me and I was

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:38.969
in the Navy. I understand about transition,
and so we work with you to make that smooth.

00:01:38.969 --> 00:01:44.189
This is a great opportunity. So jump on it.

